lesson g2-adding-tens-and-ones v=1 format=teach grade=2 unit=2 subject=maths levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Adding tens and ones"
  goal "Add and take away whole tens in your head, and find the difference between two numbers."

  look {
    scene 34x19 {
      baseten blocks thousands=0 hundreds=0 tens=4 ones=3 at=canvas(1, 1)
      comparebars bars values=[8, 5] labels=["Ann", "Ben"] difference=true below=blocks gap=2
      note n "One more ten is one more rod." width=13 right-of=blocks gap=2
    }
    say """
      Adding ten adds a whole rod and leaves the ones alone. Comparing two numbers is the gap
      between the bars, which is a subtraction.
      """
  }
  do {
    practice add.tens-and-ones count=1 seed=5
    practice add.missing-tens count=2 seed=3
    practice sub.tens-before count=1 seed=6
    practice compare.how-many-more count=1 seed=4
    practice compare.fewer-than count=2 seed=8
  }
  story {
    show barmodel.books had=34 k=5 easy-k=2 hard-k=6
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show add.balance-tens a=57 p=2 d=1 easy-a=41 easy-p=1 hard-a=69 hard-p=3 hard-d=2
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show add.triangle-tens x=15 y=25 z=10 easy-x=10 easy-y=20 easy-z=30 hard-x=35 hard-y=15 hard-z=25
  }
  remember {
    say "Add or take whole tens: the ones stay the same and only the tens change."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Base ten blocks are worth having in the house. Swapping ten ones for a rod is the exchange the
    written method rests on. In the questions about Mira and Ben, the word "more" is there but the
    answer is the smaller number; ask who has more before any sum is done. The two-star question
    can be done by working out both sides, but ask whether comparing the first numbers is quicker.
    The three-star question has no method to follow: a guess for A that is checked against the
    third box and changed by five is exactly the right way in.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level two or three tens are added or put back, the differences stay small, and the level scale moves one ten each side."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level four tens are added, the numbers reach the nineties, the level scale moves three tens against two, and the sum triangle's circles reach thirty-five."
  }
}
